alex: Quick idea — can we simplify metering for chunked/streaming requests? The sidecar + provisional claims dance is a big source of latency and makes backfills messy. Proposal: emit a lightweight reserve per chunk and a single final "commit" event that is the authoritative credit.

maya: tl;dr how does that reduce backfill pain and dupes?

alex: Commit is the single source of truth for crediting. If chunks are retried/lost we still only apply credit once when commit shows up. Backfills become: replay commit events into compact path. No cross-service RPCs per chunk.

soroush: Concern: quota checks. If we only grant on commit callers could overshoot before commit arrives.

alex: Keep a transient provisional reserve for quota checks (small debit visible to caller) but reconcile at commit. Reserves have TTL and are ignored by final accounting unless a commit references them.

jamie: How to avoid provisional_id collisions? Retries reuse req ids often.

alex: Deterministic fingerprint: sha256(tenant_id + request_fingerprint) -> provisional_parent. Each chunk writes reserve with chunk_index and deterministic provisional_id = sha256(provisional_parent + chunk_index). Commit references provisional_parent and total_tokens.

soroush: Sketch of proto?

alex: ```proto
message MeteringReserve {
  string tenant_id = 1;
  string provisional_parent = 2; // sha256(req_fingerprint)
  uint32 chunk_index = 3;
  int64 reserve_tokens = 4;
}

message MeteringCommit {
  string tenant_id = 1;
  string provisional_parent = 2;
  int64 total_tokens = 3;
  repeated Attribution attribution = 4;
}
```

maya: Ok. Two practical followups: 1) commit idempotency for replays, 2) compact path for audit-ledger.

alex: For idempotency commit includes (provisional_parent + commit_seq). Storage treats that tuple as unique; replays upsert but only first commit takes effect. Compact job materializes final ledger rows and points back to commit id.

jamie: Migration: some consumers expect per-chunk credit events today. How do we move them?

alex: Dual-write during rollout: keep emitting legacy per-chunk events while introducing reserve+commit. Provide migration script to transform commits into legacy events for consumers that can't change. Window like 6 weeks.

soroush: Performance tradeoffs: reserves increase write churn and read amplification on spikes. TTL and an in-memory hot-cache seem required. Prefer fast kv (redis) for provisional hot-path + append-only durable log for audit.

maya: Observability needs: metric for "orphaned reserves > TTL", "commit-lag p50/p95", and counts of dual-write mismatches. Also dashboard for reserve GC throughput.

ops-bot: deploy scheduled: metering-slimline v1 -> 2026-03-30T02:00Z (canary 10%).

alex: Rollout plan in RFC: flow diagram, proto, storage schema, migration steps, metrics + SLOs, backfill playbook. Owner: alex. ETA RFC: EOW.

maya: Add an operational backfill playbook: manual replay steps, detection heuristics for missing commits, and a safe-apply mode that gates high-volume replays behind rate limits.

alex: Will include. Thanks all :thumbsup:
